nfused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6283298422","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124569#issuecomment-6283298422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124569","id":6283298422,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABdoOGdg","user":{"login":"DanielKinsman","id":15639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman","html_url":"https://github.com/DanielKinsman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-20T04:20:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T04:20:27Z","body":"> _edit_ oh actually, it's more likely because in the new approach, eye offset is no longer applied, I guess if we want it to be completely accurate, we'd have to add that in too (see the new offset functions).\r\n\r\nIs that being more accurate though, with us only picking the first projection we get? I'd rather be wrong for both eyes by the same amount than correct for one and doubly wrong for the other. Do we have to make guarantees of backwards compatibility for the values coming out of these functions?\r\n\r\nOr am I misunderstanding things, is the eye offset not IPD related but something like the distance from the \"head\" tracker to the central point between both eyes?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6283298422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6306943800","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124569#issuecomment-6306943800","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124569","id":6306943800,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABd-xTOA","user":{"login":"DanielKinsman","id":15639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman","html_url":"https://github.com/DanielKinsman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-21T03:00:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T03:31:16Z","body":"Ah actually nevermind. I was doing those gdscript checks in `_ready` (frame 0) before things had warmed up and we'd got tracking data from the openxr runtime. If I do them via a `call_deferred` the outputs match between master and this PR, even without using the view offsets. At least to the amount of precision given via the print statements which round things to 6 decimal places. This is with the headset on the desk (no eye tracking) and my thumb over the presence sensor.\r\n\r\nSo I think I am happy with this  PR as is, if you are.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6306943800/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6308689867","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124569#issuecomment-6308689867","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124569","id":6308689867,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABeAb3yw","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-21T05:19:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T05:19:52Z","body":"> Or am I misunderstanding things, is the eye offset not IPD related but something like the distance from the \"head\" tracker to the central point between both eyes?\r\n\r\nYeah it's the offset between the eyes, either way though, you're never going to get anything usable out of this logic For the type of logic where these calls are used, you would generally use eye tracking and cast a ray from there.\r\nThere are no valid use cases for mapping screen location to a projected ray in XR, it just doesn't make any sense. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6308689867/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6322291386","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124569#issuecomment-6322291386","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124569","id":6322291386,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABeNaCug","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":